{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1323504-pirates-of-pugmire-some-questions-for-devs-about-missing-stuff","id":1323504,"title":"[Pirates of Pugmire] Some Questions for Devs about Missing Stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-10T13:32:01-07:00","id":1323504,"title":"[Pirates of Pugmire] Some Questions for Devs about Missing Stuff","content":"So I got a couple questions.<br /> <br /> Speed: What is the speed for Lizards and Birds? They say refer back to either Pugmire or Monarchies, but Cats and Dogs have different speeds. Dogs are faster on 4 feet. I don't think birds should have any increased speed at all as dropping to all fours is weird for birds. Lizards on the other hand should, but should they be as fast as dog or a cat? The document doesn't mention this at all.<br /> <br /> Also, Background Knacks. There is none here. Furthermore, Pugmire gives Background Tricks; Monarchies, does not, but their 'background' knacks come from their Families. Compounding on this, the two new Backgrounds do not have any Background Knacks. So how do Lizards and Birds get background knacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T16:10:35-07:00","id":1323534,"title":"","content":"Eddy's already said that we should hold off until the backer pdf errata pass at this point. Playtest feedback has been collected and is being worked into the editing process right now, so what's in the manuscript is already being adjusted and things like this should be getting addressed. We'll have another chance if they're not once things move forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T16:21:47-07:00","id":1323536,"title":"","content":"Both of those were also mentioned on the feedback form already, so I\u2019m sure Eddy will address them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T22:46:34-07:00","id":1323618,"title":"","content":"From our real playtest - which we started yesterday - we base all the stuff on <b>Mau</b>, as we have only this corebook physical and go with logical answers from there, for now.<br /> <br /> <b>So Speeds are based on the cats Speeds of <i>Mau</i></b> - 30 ft on two, 35 ft on four legs - but I was wondering how fast Sparrows would fly. as one PC in party is this? Also on 35 ft. flying then? Are Turtles slower than other Lizards? ( That was actual question of my players. ) Some clear answers in final text here are bit needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1323504-pirates-of-pugmire-some-questions-for-devs-about-missing-stuff#post1323504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do Lizards and Birds get background knacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, those <i>ARE</i> in <b>Pirates </b>beta text - those Knacks are in <i>Family / Neste Knacks </i>section, pages 21 and 22 Preview 1:<ul><li>Chameleon</li> <li>Glide</li> <li>Hunker Down</li> <li>Slither</li> <li>Soar</li> <li>Spin</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-11-2019, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T05:14:55-07:00","id":1323648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1323504-pirates-of-pugmire-some-questions-for-devs-about-missing-stuff?p=1323618#post1323618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From our real playtest - which we started yesterday - we base all the stuff on <b>Mau</b>, as we have only this corebook physical and go with logical answers from there, for now.<br /> <br /> <b>So Speeds are based on the cats Speeds of <i>Mau</i></b> - 30 ft on two, 35 ft on four legs - but I was wondering how fast Sparrows would fly. as one PC in party is this? Also on 35 ft. flying then? Are Turtles slower than other Lizards? ( That was actual question of my players. ) Some clear answers in final text here are bit needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, those <i>ARE</i> in <b>Pirates </b>beta text - those Knacks are in <i>Family / Neste Knacks </i>section, pages 21 and 22 Preview 1:<ul><li>Chameleon</li> <li>Glide</li> <li>Hunker Down</li> <li>Slither</li> <li>Soar</li> <li>Spin</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Those knacks aren\u2019t background knacks. Those are the species knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T12:21:25-07:00","id":1323748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1323504-pirates-of-pugmire-some-questions-for-devs-about-missing-stuff?p=1323648#post1323648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those knacks aren\u2019t background knacks. Those are the species knacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, those are only species knacks, which btw, are very lacking really, compared to the large amount of choices cats and dogs get with their houses/breeds. Lizards and birds seem kinda side characters in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T12:22:41-07:00","id":1323749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1323504-pirates-of-pugmire-some-questions-for-devs-about-missing-stuff?p=1323534#post1323534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eddy's already said that we should hold off until the backer pdf errata pass at this point. Playtest feedback has been collected and is being worked into the editing process right now, so what's in the manuscript is already being adjusted and things like this should be getting addressed. We'll have another chance if they're not once things move forward.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was merely asking suggestions until the next round comes out. I don't think cats should model bird speeds at all, as the thought of birds getting on all fours was... well... kinda silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T21:10:13-07:00","id":1323851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1323504-pirates-of-pugmire-some-questions-for-devs-about-missing-stuff?p=1323748#post1323748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, those are only species knacks, which btw, are very lacking really, compared to the large amount of choices cats and dogs get with their houses/breeds. Lizards and birds seem kinda side characters in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Pirates </b>are <i>sourcebook</i>, not new corebook in the lines. From what I got in interviews of Eddy, <b>Pugmire</b> and <b>Mau</b> are proper games in <b>Realms</b> universe - rest of species are just small add-on. Think of it as ( nWoD ) <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> 1E - we have whole game line <b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b>. And we have only one sourcebook for all the other were-something <b>Changing Breeds</b>. <b>Werewolf</b> is gameline, <b>Changing Breeds</b> are just supplements. Same here - <b>Pugmire</b> and <b>Mau </b>are gamelines, <b>Pirates</b> is just supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}